 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It' not that random. Think of it like this. In German, gendered words for things that are usually male or female tend to end in a different ending than gender neutral words. It is. So if you want to know a word's gender, look at its ending. That said, there are some big exceptions that throw off the pattern. For example, the word for door, Tür, is female, even though doors themselves are usually male. It comes from the bright side of the door being the female part in German architecture. It is, but it' true. The system isn't perfect, but memorizing these patterns can help. Most people do. The key is practice. The more you use the system, the easier it gets.",
